The person has no prompt yet. They gave documents about their work and, maybe, an end goal. Write a prompt that
makes a model do that work well, using what the documents say (rules, terms, formats, examples).

system_template: the standing instructions: the role, the rules from the documents, the output format, what to do
when the answer is not in the input. Plain language. Do not paste the documents; use their rules.
user_template: only what a real user supplies on each request, such as their question. The knowledge from the
documents belongs in system_template, never as an input to fill in. Put each input in double braces, for example {{ "{{ question }}" }}.
variables: the names used in user_template, lowercase with underscores.
reasons: one short sentence per important choice, saying which part of the documents it came from.
If there is no end goal, work out the most likely task from the documents and say so in the first reason.

